The magnetic pressure on the plane at \(x=d\) is determined by the discontinuity of the magnetic stress tensor across the surface. Using the fields that satisfy the wave‑equation in the slab and the boundary conditions at \(x=0\) and \(x=d\), the resulting time‑averaged normal stress is  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle 
\vec f \;=\; \hat{\imath}_x \,\frac{1}{2}\,
\frac{\mu_{0}\,K_{0}^{2}\,\cos^{2}(\omega t)}
{\cosh^{2}\!\left(\frac{\omega_{p}\,d}{c}\right)}\;
\exp\!\left(-\frac{\omega d}{c}\right)}
\]

which corresponds to choice **E**.<|return|>

A) \displaystyle \mathbf{E}(r<R_{p})=-\frac{\mathbf{P}_{0}}{3\varepsilon_{0}} 

B) \displaystyle \mathbf{E}(R_{p}<r<R)=-\frac{\mathbf{P}_{0}}{3\varepsilon_{0}}\frac{R_{p}^{3}}{r^{3}} 

C) \displaystyle \mathbf{E}(r=R)=0 

D) \displaystyle \mathbf{D}(r<R_{p})=\varepsilon_{0}\mathbf{E}+\mathbf{P}_{0}=0 

E) \displaystyle \mathbf{D}(R_{p}<r<R)=\varepsilon_{0}\mathbf{E}=-\frac{\mathbf{P}_{0}R_{p}^{3}}{3r^{3}}.<|return|>
